  partName: IntakeManifoldBoltCenterLeft (3)
  description: The IntakeManifoldBoltCenterLeft (3) is a tiny, elongated bolt located
    at the top-left-center of the engine, playing a crucial role in securing the
    intake manifold to the engine block. Its Material.001 composition provides excellent
    strength and durability, while its small size allows it to fit into tight spaces.
    Notably, the IntakeManifoldBoltCenterLeft (3) is the third in a series of bolts
    that work together to ensure a secure and stable intake manifold, highlighting
    the engine's redundant design philosophy.
